// RFC 5961 3.2 / Linux: an RST at RCV.NXT closes the connection; another in-window
// RST gets a challenge ACK and the connection survives. The first reset is proven by
// a new SYN-ACK on the same 4-tuple. After the second RST, more data must echo, then
// an exact-sequence RST permits another handshake. ISNs and scaled window:
// see handshake-linux-options.pkt and echo-and-close.pkt.

0     < S 0:0(0) win 64240 <mss 1460,nop,nop,sackOK,nop,wscale 7>
+0    > S. 0:0(0) ack 1 win 65535 <mss 1460,wscale 2,sackOK,eol,eol,eol>
+0    < . 1:1(0) ack 1 win 502
+0    < P. 1:11(10) ack 1 win 502
+0    > P. 1:11(10) ack 11 win 32768
+0    < . 11:11(0) ack 11 win 502
+0    < R. 11:11(0) ack 11 win 0

+0.1  < S 5000:5000(0) win 64240 <mss 1460,nop,nop,sackOK,nop,wscale 7>
+0    > S. 0:0(0) ack 5001 win 65535 <mss 1460,wscale 2,sackOK,eol,eol,eol>
+0    < . 5001:5001(0) ack 1 win 502
+0    < P. 5001:5011(10) ack 1 win 502
+0    > P. 1:11(10) ack 5011 win 32768
+0    < . 5011:5011(0) ack 11 win 502
+0    < R. 6011:6011(0) ack 11 win 0
+0    > . 11:11(0) ack 5011 win 32768
+0    < P. 5011:5021(10) ack 11 win 502
+0    > P. 11:21(10) ack 5021 win 32768
+0    < . 5021:5021(0) ack 21 win 502
+0    < R. 5021:5021(0) ack 21 win 0

+0.1  < S 9000:9000(0) win 64240 <mss 1460,nop,nop,sackOK,nop,wscale 7>
+0    > S. 0:0(0) ack 9001 win 65535 <mss 1460,wscale 2,sackOK,eol,eol,eol>
